Hi,

On Monday 21 June 2010, Agustin Lobo wrote:
> Is it possible to include text in the output

you can use
  rk.header(), rk.print(), and rk.print.literal()
. If you need more specific formatting, you can also use
  .rk.cat.output()
which allows adding raw HTML code.

> (and then save it
> as html including graphics that have been sent
> to the output)?

Actually, ATM, the easiest way to export the output including the graphics is 
to copy the files from ~/.rkward/ (files rk_out.html and graph*.png/svg/jpg). 

For any other output format besides HTML, selecting everything and 
copying/pasting into OpenOffice works pretty well.

Regards
Thomas
